    "variant_group": "warden_hello_02",
    "variant": 5,
    "source_locale": "en",
    "text_key": "lore.warden_hello_02_v05.text"
  },
  {
    "id": "warden_hello_02_v06",
    "speaker": "milewarden",
    "event": "greeting",
    "condition": "Any",
    "text": "Good to see a fellow Milewarden. Have you found a way to make paper ignore the weather?",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "variant_group": "warden_hello_02",
    "variant": 6,
    "source_locale": "en",
    "text_key": "lore.warden_hello_02_v06.text"
  },
  {
    "id": "warden_neighbors_01",
    "speaker": "milewarden",
    "event": "topic_neighbors",
    "condition": "Any",
    "text": "An old border can outlive the kingdom that drew it. I ask the neighbors what they call a place before I put ink on the map.",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "variant_group": "warden_neighbors_01",
    "variant": 1,
    "source_locale": "en",
    "text_key": "lore.warden_neighbors_01.text"
  },
  {
    "id": "warden_neighbors_01_v02",
    "speaker": "milewarden",
    "event": "topic_neighbors",
    "condition": "Any",
    "text": "Before I copy an old border, I ask who lives on each side of it.",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "variant_group": "warden_neighbors_01",
    "variant": 2,
    "source_locale": "en",
    "text_key": "lore.warden_neighbors_01_v02.text"
  },
  {
    "id": "warden_neighbors_01_v03",
    "speaker": "milewarden",
    "event": "topic_neighbors",
    "condition": "Any",
    "text": "A kingdom can vanish while its boundary stones remain. The neighbors still have to get along.",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "variant_group": "warden_neighbors_01",
    "variant": 3,
    "source_locale": "en",
    "text_key": "lore.warden_neighbors_01_v03.text"
  },
  {
    "id": "warden_neighbors_01_v04",
    "speaker": "milewarden",
    "event": "topic_neighbors",
    "condition": "Any",
    "text": "Two neighbors may name a place differently. My map has room for both names.",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "variant_group": "warden_neighbors_01",
    "variant": 4,
    "source_locale": "en",
    "text_key": "lore.warden_neighbors_01_v04.text"
  },
  {
    "id": "warden_neighbors_01_v05",
    "speaker": "milewarden",
    "event": "topic_neighbors",
    "condition": "Any",
    "text": "I write down what the people here call their country. Old rulers rarely answer follow-up questions.",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "variant_group": "warden_neighbors_01",
    "variant": 5,
    "source_locale": "en",
    "text_key": "lore.warden_neighbors_01_v05.text"
  },
  {
    "id": "warden_neighbors_01_v06",
    "speaker": "milewarden",
    "event": "topic_neighbors",
    "condition": "Any",
    "text": "A border on old paper is worth asking about. So are the households it crosses.",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "variant_group": "warden_neighbors_01",
    "variant": 6,
    "source_locale": "en",
    "text_key": "lore.warden_neighbors_01_v06.text"
  },
  {
